==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Rabbit Champion Satoru''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Rabbit Satoru is an anti-Traitless version of his [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|counterpart]] trading his Surge Immunity for Wave Immunity.

In terms of general stats, Rabbit Satoru is pretty decent. His DPS of 3.6k is below standard for his range, but his large pierce makes up for it by allowing him to chip away at enemies you couldn't normally hit. Of course, Rabbit Satoru has his downsides. For one, he has abysmal health with only two repositions, making him sort of a glass cannon. He also has a long attack animation combined with his noticeably small inner range and large blindspot, meaning aggressive enemies can enter his blindspot before having the chance to attack. His Wave Immunity is also very situational. Ideally, units like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]], [[Gloomy Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Costumed Witchy Neneko]] or other [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Blockers]] are enough to block waves entirely; however if this isn't fathomable, the frontline tends to shift quite a lot and can easily leave Rabbit Satoru completely vulnerable if precaution isn't enforced.

In terms of abilities, Rabbit Satoru's slow has just above a guaranteed 50% uptime, granting him good crowd control. Moreover, his short cooldown and minimal cost allows him to stack for an even higher uptime, and when combined with his 400 pierce range, he can effectively halt nearly all Traitless enemies on field. His Wave Immunity can be very helpful against Traitless enemies specifically as many have Waves, such as Mr. Mer, [[Crazed Gross Cat (Enemy)|Crazed]]/[[Manic Macho Legs (Enemy)|Manic Macho Legs]], [[Kory]] and [[Hermit Cat (Enemy)|Hermit Cat]]. Along with previously mentioned weaknesses hindering his ability potential, Rabbit Satoru's crowd control has its problems. The biggest and most unavoidable is the existence of a vast amount of Traitless enemies that can pierce. [[Mr. Mole]], [[Dolphina]], [[Henry]] and [[Croakley]], which usually are present in many Traitless only levels, are all able to flank Rabbit Satoru and make him completely useless. Another problem is without a strong frontline, enemies such as [[Rain D.]], [[R.Ost]], [[Bore Jr.]] and [[Wild Doge]] can reach him easily and waste a reposition.

In closing, if you happen to have [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Mitama]] or any other Traitless crowd control, this unit can be safely skipped. If not, Rabbit Satoru can prove to be a powerful support unit in your arsenal.

{{Job|Classification = Backliner & Crowd-Controller}}

